# Shell scripts must stay LF. They run under bash — WSL, the release Macs, and
# EAS's Linux workers — where a trailing CR makes line 14 of publish-ios.sh read
# as `set: pipefail\r: invalid option name` and the release aborts before it
# starts. Without this, core.autocrlf=true on a Windows clone checks them out
# with CRLF and they are broken on arrival.
*.sh text eol=lf
